// A wellformedness TOPIC that closes and reopens, inside the run of checks
// around it.
//
// HS `checkWellformedness` (Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:1270-1286) is one
// ordered list of checks (lines 1272-1282), and `formulaReports`
// (Wellformedness.hs:999-1014) is a single one of them.  Inside it, `msum
// [checkQuantifiers, checkTerms, checkGuarded]` (lines 1002-1004) runs on
// EVERY annotated formula; `WfErrorReport` is a list, so `msum` is `concat`
// and all three arms report unconditionally, per formula, in item order.
// `prettyWfErrorReport` (Wellformedness.hs:118-125) then groups with `groupOn
// fst` (line 120), which is `groupBy ((==) `on` fst)` (Extension/Prelude.hs:96-97)
// and merges only CONSECUTIVE entries.  A topic therefore gets a second
// underlined header when another topic falls between its findings:
//
//   - `Redu` and `Redu2` both trip `checkTerms` and `NoGuard` trips
//     `checkGuarded` between them, so "Formula terms" closes around
//     " Formula guardedness" and opens again.  Collecting a topic's findings
//     into one block instead gives a single header and reorders the bodies;
//   - `RQ` trips `checkQuantifiers` (Wellformedness.hs:948-957).  Its entry
//     sits with the formula it came from, not with its topic: `annFormulas`
//     (Wellformedness.hs:1007-1014) is `lemmas <|> restrictions`, so the
//     restriction's block follows every lemma's, after the reopened one.
//
// The two bracketing entries are what pin the whole run's POSITION: the rule's
// free `u` trips `unboundReport` (Wellformedness.hs:514-519) from an earlier
// check, and the reusable exists-trace lemma trips `lemmaAttributeReport`
// (Wellformedness.hs:924-932) from the next one.  RS reaches `formulaReports`
// only after the parser-level pass — the arms need the elaborated signature
// and the translated theory — and splices its findings into that report, so
// without an entry on each side the splice lands at the end whatever anchor
// list it uses and its position says nothing.
//
// No corpus theory reaches this: not one corpus wf block carries a repeated
// topic header, a "Quantifier sorts" header or a " Formula guardedness"
// header.
//
// Compared slices: the wf report block (see check.sh).  Every offender list
// here fits the report's ribbon without a break, so what the fixture answers
// for is the order of the headers and their bodies, not the fills.

theory WfTopicInterleave
begin

builtins: diffie-hellman

rule R:
  [ In( x ) ] --[ A( x ) ]-> [ Out( <x, u> ) ]

lemma Redu:
  "All x #i. A(x^x) @ i ==> F"

lemma NoGuard:
  "All z. z = z"

lemma Redu2:
  "All y #j. A(y^y) @ j ==> F"

lemma Reuse [reuse]:
  exists-trace "Ex x #i. A(x) @ #i"

restriction RQ:
  "All ~q #i. A(~q) @ i ==> F"

end
